quantiles_depth_augmented mean 0.4841  sd 0.0223
quantiles_flank_v1     mean 0.4954  sd 0.0229

unpaired  (wrong)     gap +0.0113 against a fold sd of ~0.0223, Welch p = 0.0138
paired    (optimistic) mean difference +0.0113  sd 0.0070  95% CI [+0.0094, +0.0133]  t = 11.48  p = 0.0000  wins 48/50
corrected (quote this) 95% CI [+0.0040, +0.0186]  t = 3.12  p = 0.0030

The corrected row is Nadeau & Bengio: it inflates the variance to admit
that each fold's model trains on the other 4, so the observations are not
independent. Its p-value is always the larger of the two, and it is the one to
quote - a difference that only clears 0.05 uncorrected has not cleared it.

quantiles_flank_v1 is +0.0113 better than quantiles_depth_augmented, winning 48/50 paired observations, corrected p = 0.0030. Consistent in direction and significant even after correcting for the overlap between training sets.

